{"id": "EUVD-2026-103659", "enisaUuid": "12b8ca58-882a-35b2-9b77-53f7f83d6a82", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsctp: avoid livelock while updating retransmit path\n\nsctp_assoc_update_retran_path() can loop forever when every remaining\ntransport, including retran_path, is SCTP_UNCONFIRMED: the state check\nruns before the wraparound test, so the loop cannot observe that it has\ncompleted a full pass.\n\nFix this by considering a transport only when it is not UNCONFIRMED,\nthen checking whether the walk has returned to retran_path. This makes\nthe full-pass termination independent of the transport state while\npreserving the existing fallback selection semantics.\n\nAlso restore the NULL guard around the retran_path assignment. In the\nall-UNCONFIRMED case there is no eligible replacement transport, and\ninstalling NULL would leave later retransmit-path users and the debug\nprint with a NULL path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:42", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3fe624c3843694ab096fdb198526ba0c659febbe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43410c1f2db53516e95ddd7e5b4b02f495b78121", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d893a7cc1cb41dd510f338bb2bfd8f29b14eaf49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83b1a7f9e718828ef364a7b004254ebb2d0035fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/173610fff55022a5ad1579fbcc7faa97467b58b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9338057df1025f578fe7d0ff08bada87b8b838d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ddc34cc0834c873871e88b055ee6a260676efe97", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2c31b837406395e576afeb25958c98e9938f3f6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hjhx-c2pg-c62c", "CVE-2026-98614"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13251053-9fa0-34d1-8261-00e0daf04815", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.12.71 <3.13"}, {"id": "2a46d3cb-f3ba-35a5-bd01-0be1c6b6ea39", "product": {"